I can't decide what is my favorite but I think it might be the Pisa shirt. Cuz it's leaning, it's a leaning face of Pisa.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.980
Part 3: a story from my recent past. So Hank, I don't like to drop names or anything,

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.180
but after I got meningitis last year Bill Gates sent me a 'get well soon' orchid.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:42.060
It was a really thoughtful gesture and I really appreciated it. So anyway, recently we had a dinner party at our house and someone said "I LOVE your orchid!"

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.840
and I said "I know, it's beautiful, right? Not to name drop or anything, but Bill Gates gave it to me."

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.920
and everyone was like "oh, that's very impressive, a Bill Gates orchid."

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.940
Except Sarah was looking at me kind of funny so I was like "What?" and she was like "oh, it's nothing," and I was like "WHAT?"

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:59.640
and she was like "well, I mean... that's not Bill Gates's orchid." And I was like "What do you mean it's not Bill Gates's orchid!?"

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.660
And she was like "Bill Gates's orchid died. We got this orchid at Trader Joe's."

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.940
So I was a little bit embarrassed but you know I'm not a particularly observant person when it comes to orchids.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:14.420
So anyway, flash forward a couple week, my friend Stuart, seen here with his wife Anne-Marie and the orchid in question, brings me a gift and I unwrap it...

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:19.020
and it's a little plaque for my orchid. To remind me, you know, that's not Bill Gates's orchid.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.660
Anyway Hank what I'm saying is that I have great friends. This is a double bragging story, because first I'm bragging about the Bill Gates orchid

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.800
